motor_snapshots schema reference: migrations/000170_snapshots_si.up.sql lines 125-166.
DiAxleSpeed* are RPM (field-natural unit, UnitKindNone, no SI conversion via normalize.toSI;
see column comment at migrations/000170_snapshots_si.up.sql:182-183).
DiTorque* / DiVBat / DiMotorCurrent* are also UnitKindNone (Tesla emits them already in SI).
DiHeatsinkT* / DiInverterT* / DiStatorTemp* are UnitKindTemperature and pass through normalize.toSI
so Setting*Unit observers convert F->C before writing.
Hvil + DiState* are enums; the motor_snapshot writer (added in a later prompt) maps
them to their TEXT column via protomodel enum parsers.
No also_signal_log dual-write on any powertrain field: motor_snapshots is itself the
SI-canonical history (hypertable, 7-day chunks) so signal_log replication would be
redundant. cagg_battery_daily sources from charging signals, not powertrain.

Insertion points (case-sensitive ASCII alphabetical, matching existing yaml ordering):
  - 34 Di* entries between 'DetailedChargeState' and 'DriveRail'
  - Hvil between 'HvacSteeringWheelHeatLevel' and 'IdealBatteryRange'
  - IsolationResistance between 'InsideTemp' and 'LateralAcceleration'

